WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.240
This video was sponsored by The Purge on USA
Network, a ten episode television event premiering

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:06.580
on Tuesday, September 4.

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:09.020
Will you hide, or will you seek?

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:13.940
Tune in to USA Network every Tuesday to make
your choice...and seal your fate.

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:20.800
You don't need us to tell you that there's
too much to watch these days..

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:26.300
Even months before Halloween, 2018 had already
delivered a number of standout horror movies,

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:29.100
many of them flying under the radar - so we've
collected our favorites.

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:32.920
For one reason or another, all of them were
overlooked, but they're all worth a second

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:33.420
chance.

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:34.980
Terrifier

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:39.860
Sometimes a horror fan wants something intellectual,
and sometimes you just want to watch people

00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:41.260
run from an insane clown.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:46.280
Trashy, exploitative, and mean-spirited, Terrifier
is the sort of movie that's meant to be discovered

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:47.720
on a beat-up VHS tape.

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:52.070
Except instead of being pumped out into dollar
theaters in the '80s, it was somehow released

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:53.220
in 2018.

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:56.340
Terrifier commits to its trashiness from every
angle.

00:00:56.700 --> 00:01:00.760
It's simplistic, low-budget, and sometimes
dubiously acted - which is not to say that

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:01.480
it's a bad movie.

00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:06.320
While it's certainly not for everybody, the
movie has notched a solid 80 percent on Rotten

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:10.760
Tomatoes, meaning slasher fans should feel
confident giving this punchy thrill ride a

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:11.260
late-night spin.

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:12.560
Pyewacket

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:17.640
What if you made a nasty wish in a fit of
rage, only to find later that you couldn't

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:18.340
take it back?

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:23.000
Pyewacket tells the story of a teenage girl
who naively puts a curse on her mother in

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:24.200
a half-baked woodsy ritual.

00:01:24.690 --> 00:01:28.740
After her moment of frustration has passed,
the girl has to watch as her curse becomes

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:32.080
terrifyingly real, and the consequences close
in around her.

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:37.190
Pyewacket is a movie from the slow burn school
of horror, favoring mood over scary moments

00:01:37.190 --> 00:01:39.120
and a sense of dread over jump scares.

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:44.120
Elevated by strong performances from its mother
and daughter leads, the movie sports a concept

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:48.850
relatable to anyone who's ever been a teenager
- especially a teenager who's made a big mistake

00:01:48.850 --> 00:01:49.340
or two.

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:50.660
Wildling

00:01:50.980 --> 00:01:55.780
Wildling isn't just an underappreciated horror
movie - this unsung character study is one

00:01:55.780 --> 00:01:57.080
of the best movies of the year.

00:01:57.310 --> 00:02:01.900
The story of a young woman raised in captivity
who enters the real world as a teenager, it's

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:05.060
a feral child story that takes its premise
very literally.

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:09.959
A supernatural horror movie, Wildling brings
out its fantastical elements slowly, drawing

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:14.180
you into its world of believable characters
well before it reveals what it really is.

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:18.290
It's a movie that tests your allegiances as
a viewer, with your sympathies constantly

00:02:18.290 --> 00:02:20.420
shifting as the circumstances change.

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:25.140
It's also a movie of adolescent self-discovery
with a particularly wild twist.

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:29.840
Starting like a supernatural version of the
movie Room, Wildling basically turns into

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:33.740
Predator by its third act - an appropriate
transformation, given the subject matter.

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:35.080
Revenge

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:39.880
Left for dead in an isolated location, a young
woman is forced to hang on to her life as

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:43.100
the criminals who nearly did her in come back
to finish her off for good.

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:47.920
Over the course of Revenge she turns from
a carefree hedonist into a vengeful destroyer.

00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:53.060
The circumstances of her near-death experience
are so brutal and unfair; you've never wanted

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:56.110
to see the bad guys get what's coming to them
as badly as you do here.

00:02:56.220 --> 00:03:01.180
A vicious, adrenaline-pumping look at savagery
and survival, Revenge is not a comfortable

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:05.400
watch, basically being a cross between 127
Hours and I Spit on Your Grave.

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:08.640
But if you've got the guts to watch it, it's
a trip well worth

00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:09.240
your time.

00:03:09.780 --> 00:03:11.700
The Strangers: Prey at Night

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:16.420
A surprise hit when it invaded theaters in
2008, it took the producers of The Strangers

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:18.500
a decade for a follow-up to be realized.

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:23.060
Enthusiasm for the first movie faded in the
time between releases, and the sequel landed

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:25.180
in theaters with a much more muted splash.

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:29.340
But fans of the original Strangers shouldn't
ignore this second go-around, which may be

00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:30.440
better than the original.

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:35.220
Moving the action from a couple's home to
an empty trailer park, Prey at Night effectively

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:38.360
builds on the original's premise of pointless,
random violence.

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:41.120
It can't be reasoned with - it can only be
fled.

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:45.120
The sequel gains points over the original
for the target family's tendency to fight

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:48.950
back, making the game of cat-and-mouse much
more of a level playing field than it was

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:52.560
in the original, and ultimately, making this
a more rewarding watch.

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:53.940
Mom and Dad

00:03:54.320 --> 00:03:58.120
Written and directed by Brian Taylor, one
half of the directing duo that brought the

00:03:58.129 --> 00:04:02.499
world the Crank movies, Mom and Dad is a look
at the most out-of-hand family squabble you've

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:03.260
ever seen.

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:06.900
It's as though they took a mundane argument
between parents and their children, added

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:09.840
Nicolas Cage, and… well, made a Crank movie
out of it.

00:04:09.960 --> 00:04:14.380
Simple and brutal, Mom and Dad is a cathartic
and chaotic horror-comedy, with all the best

00:04:14.389 --> 00:04:19.100
Nicolas Cage weirdness you could ask for - up
to and including an enraged performance of

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:20.500
the Hokey Pokey that involves a sledgehammer.

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:25.091
It's not every filmgoer's favorite flavor,
but if you're still with this video, you're

00:04:25.091 --> 00:04:26.390
probably the target audience.

